  "question": {
    "text": "Three identical blocks of masses $\\mathrm{m}=2 \\mathrm{~kg}$ are drawn by a force $\\mathrm{F}=10.2 \\mathrm{~N}$ with an acceleration of $0.6 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-2}$ on a frictions surface, then what is the tension (in $\\mathrm{N}$ ) in the string between the blocks $B$ and $C$?\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/gLO7HRu6Kcb6dFSAguDZRj-be6KFr7Jx8MIXOZlA2vo.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "H57mV",
      "text": "\n9.2\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Jd3kV",
      "text": "\n7.8\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "p85mU",
      "text": "\n4\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NCSqQ",
      "text": "\n9.8",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Apply Newton's second law\n$$\n\\mathrm{F}-\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{ab}}=m a ; \\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{ab}}-\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{bc}}=\\mathrm{ma} \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{bc}}=7.8 \\mathrm{~N}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
